another problem:
 https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/7ab754d9973e7b7481658bd937e186362f603f70/subsys/bluetooth/mesh/transport.c#L1483-L1490
while in `seg_rx_alloc` allocate all segment, but not to check return value of `k_mem_slab_alloc`, so, if  no buf available, the `rx->seg[j]` will be set to 'NULL',
 https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/7ab754d9973e7b7481658bd937e186362f603f70/subsys/bluetooth/mesh/transport.c#L1676 will be cause set to zero-point, and finally to be dead.

### Suggestion

allocation for each segment when received such mesh segment message.
``` C
	if (!k_delayed_work_remaining_get(&rx->ack) &&
	    !bt_mesh_lpn_established()) {
		k_delayed_work_submit(&rx->ack, ack_timeout(rx));
	}

        err = k_mem_slab_alloc(&rx->seg[seg_o]);
        if (err) {
                 /* will be ability to receive later or just call seg_rx_reset here */
                return err;
        }

	memcpy(rx->seg[seg_o], buf->data, buf->len);
```
